TITLE:: SeqPat
SUMMARY:: A pattern that plays one named sequence from a Sequencer.
CATEGORIES:: Streams-Patterns-Events
RELATED:: Classes/Pattern, Classes/Sequencer

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::SeqPat:: is the LINK::Classes/Pattern:: returned by LINK::Classes/Sequencer#-pat::. It stores that sequencer and a sequence id. LINK::Classes/Pseq::, LINK::Classes/Ppar::, and the other list patterns can embed it. When the pattern plays, it looks the id up on the sequencer. A MIDI sequence is wrapped with that sequence's pre-keys, post-keys, and MIDI route. A composition is embedded as stored, so each nested TELETYPE::SeqPat:: wraps its own leaf. A missing id throws. A cycle throws.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a TELETYPE::SeqPat:: for one sequence id.

ARGUMENT:: sequencer
The LINK::Classes/Sequencer:: that holds the named sequence.

ARGUMENT:: id
A LINK::Classes/Symbol::. The sequence does not need to exist yet.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::SeqPat::.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: embedInStream
Looks CODE::id:: up on the stored sequencer and embeds that sequence.

ARGUMENT:: inval
The input event, as for any LINK::Classes/Pattern::.

RETURNS::
The event returned by the embedded sequence.

METHOD:: id
The sequence LINK::Classes/Symbol:: this pattern names.

RETURNS::
A LINK::Classes/Symbol::.

PRIVATE:: init
